.TH "goblinctl" "1" "Jan 1970" "goblinctl 0.1.0-proto2g" "General Commands Manual"

.SH NAME
goblinctl-cluster-migrate-instance - Live-migrate a running instance to another node (CRIU)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgoblinctl cluster migrate-instance   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Live-migrate a running instance to another node.

.PP
The instance is checkpointed on its current node, its memory image is
transferred, and it is restored on the destination under the same
instance UUID. The process keeps its state; only its location changes.

.PP
If any step fails the instance is restored on its source and the
migration is reported as rolled back. If the rollback also fails the
instance is running nowhere, and the error says so explicitly.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for migrate-instance


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--control-addr\fP=""
	Address of the target daemon's control plane (empty: from config)

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP=""
	Log level: debug, info, warn, error

.PP
\fB--tls-ca\fP=""
	CA certificate used to verify the daemon

.PP
\fB--tls-insecure\fP[=false]
	Skip verification (INSECURE)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--version\fP[=false]
	version for goblinctl


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgoblinctl-cluster(1)\fP
